  "body": "The font WOFF 2.0 is a W3C **Candidate** Recommendation for a font as defined https://www.w3.org/TR/WOFF2/\r\n\r\nAlthough this is still a candidate recommendation (since 15th March 2016), is there any possibility to have this added to the mimesniff specification? It's widely supported, in most modern browsers: http://caniuse.com/#feat=woff2. Having support here, helps web servers sniff this type and set the correct content type headers.\r\n\r\nThe header is defined: https://www.w3.org/TR/WOFF2/#woff20Header as `77 4F 46 32` (the string \"wOF2\"), and the mime type `font/woff2` https://www.w3.org/TR/WOFF2/#IMT (also discussed in #23).\r\n\r\nI'd be happy to PR this if you like.",
